Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Keep the pillarbox of scaled fullscreen windows.

The client rect of a frameless fullscreen window was replaced by its visible
rect, to drop frame insets left over from separate WindowPos updates. With an
emulated display mode the visible rect covers the whole monitor while the
window keeps the aspect ratio of the mode (an 800x600 window is pillarboxed at
(480,0)-(3360,2160) on a 3840x2160 monitor), so the client surface was
stretched over the whole output.

Without a frame the client area is the window rect, use that instead. It is
the visible rect for other fullscreen windows.
---

--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
@@ -292,10 +292,14 @@
     }
 
     /* A frame removal and fullscreen resize may arrive in separate WindowPos
-     * updates, leaving the cached client rect with the old frame insets. */
+     * updates, leaving the cached client rect with the old frame insets.
+     * Without a frame the client area is the window rect, which is not the
+     * visible rect when an exclusive fullscreen window keeps the aspect
+     * ratio of an emulated display mode (e.g. an 800x600 mode pillarboxed on
+     * a 3840x2160 monitor). */
     if ((window_state & WAYLAND_SURFACE_CONFIG_STATE_FULLSCREEN) &&
         !(style & (WS_CAPTION | WS_THICKFRAME)))
-        conf->client_rect = conf->rect;
+        conf->client_rect = conf->window_rect;
 
     conf->resizeable = (style & WS_THICKFRAME) && !fullscreen;
     conf->state = window_state;
